```markdown
---
description: Template for creating new project plan files with PMT schema
globs: ["**/*plan*.md", "**/*projekt*.md", "**/*project*.md", "**/*overview*.md"]
alwaysApply: false
---

## New Project File Rule

When creating a NEW project plan or overview markdown file, ALWAYS start with
the PMT frontmatter schema. Do not skip fields.

### Ask the user these questions in ONE message before creating the file

```
Bevor ich die Datei anlege, brauche ich folgende Infos:

1. Projektname (kurz, kebab-case)?
2. Kurzbeschreibung (1–2 Sätze)?
3. Typ: saas / software / tool / research / internal?
4. Status: idea / active / on_hold / launched / maintenance / archived?
5. Phase: ideation / validation / build / release / operation?
6. Phase-Fortschritt in %?
7. Nächster Milestone (Titel)?
8. Zieldatum für Milestone (optional)?
```

### Then create the file with this frontmatter

```yaml
---
name: [user input]
overview: [user input]
isProject: true
pmt_id: [generate UUID v4]

type: [user input]
tags: []

status: [user input]
phase: [user input]
phase_progress: [user input]
current_version: ~
next_milestone: [user input]
milestone_due: [user input or ~]
on_hold_reason: ~

last_activity: [today YYYY-MM-DD]

todos: []

schema_version: "1.0"
---

# [Project Name]

## Überblick

[overview text]

## Todos

<!-- Tasks hier als Checkboxen mit #high / #medium / #low Tags -->

```

### After creating
- Confirm frontmatter was added correctly
- Remind user: "Vergiss nicht, diesen Dateipfad im PMT zu registrieren."
```

✅ Fertig — der Agent erstellt neue Dateien ab jetzt immer im richtigen Format.

